1
00:05:28,421 --> 00:05:34,421
The most dangerous man in the world. He's about to expose
the CIA, the FBI, the KGB ... and himself.

2
00:10:56,842 --> 00:11:02,842
Hopscotch is a comedy, adventure film directed by Ronald Neame.

3
00:16:25,263 --> 00:16:31,263
When CIA operative Miles Kendig deliberately lets KGB agent
Yaskov get away, his boss threatens to retire him.

4
00:21:53,684 --> 00:21:59,684
Kendig beats him to it, however, destroying his own records and traveling to Austria where he
begins work on a memoir that will expose all his former agency's covert practices.

5
00:27:22,105 --> 00:27:28,105
The CIA catches wind of the book and sends other agents after him,
initiating a frenetic game of cat and mouse that spans the globe.

6
00:32:50,526 --> 00:32:56,526
Miles Kendig, played by Walter Matthau.

7
00:38:18,947 --> 00:38:24,947
Isobel, played by Glenda Jackson.

8
00:43:47,368 --> 00:43:53,368
Jack Cutter, played by Sam Waterston.

9
00:49:15,789 --> 00:49:21,789
Myerson, played by Ned Beatty.

10
00:54:44,210 --> 00:54:50,210
Yaskov, played by Herbert Lom.

11
01:00:12,631 --> 01:00:18,631
Ross, played by David Matthau.

12
01:05:41,052 --> 01:05:47,052
Hopscotch is a 1980 American comedy spy film directed by Ronald Neame and starring
Walter Matthau, Glenda Jackson, Sam Waterston, Ned Beatty and Herbert Lom.

13
01:11:09,473 --> 01:11:15,473
The screenplay was written by Bryan Forbes and Brian
Garfield, based on Garfield's 1975 novel.

14
01:16:37,894 --> 01:16:43,894
Garfield took the title of his book from the children's playground game, "wherein a player has
to retrieve 'an elusive object' while hopping on a sidewalk from space to space.

15
01:22:06,315 --> 01:22:12,315
One false step or clumsy move could mean falling and landing on one's backside."
Matthau's performance received a
Golden Globe nomination for Best Actor – Motion Picture Musical or Comedy at the 38th Golden Globe Awards.

16
01:27:34,736 --> 01:27:40,736
In 2002, the Criterion Collection released the film on DVD,
followed by a 2K restoration on Blu-ray in 2017.

17
01:33:03,157 --> 01:33:09,157
The film explores themes of central intelligence agency (cia),
based on novel or book, england, germany, spy.

18
01:38:31,578 --> 01:38:37,578
The tone is lighthearted.
